  "facts": [
    "The Dos Valires Tunnel, stretching 2.922 kilometres, links Generals Roads 2 and 3, bridging the Valira del Nord and Valira d'Orient valleys in Andorra.",
    "Construction began in 2005 but halted in 2009 after a viaduct collapse that claimed five Portuguese workers, marking a tragic pause in the tunnel’s development.",
    "Since 2022, cyclists can ride both directions inside the tunnel, with mandatory front white and rear red lighting, plus the first 200 metres of the cycle lane now painted green for safety."
